female with median age at death of 87 years (IQR:80-92).
Dementia was diagnosed antemortem in 57%. About 55%
had Braak stage V-VI and 61% had Thal amyloid- β phase
≥3. Fifty-two percent met criteria for intermediate-high prob-
ability AD. TDP-43-immunoreactivity (TDP-43(+)) was
detected in 44% of the cohort (median stage 3[IQR:1-5]),
and in 54% of dementia subgroup (median stage 3
[IQR:2-5]). TDP-43(+) frequency and distribution increased
with age at death. At 70 years at death, an estimated 30%
(95% CI:25%-35%) of the cohort was TDP-43(+) versus
33% (CI:27%-39%) of dementia subgroup. By 90 years,
49% (CI:45%-52%) of the cohort and 67% (CI:62%-72%)
