Background: Dementia with Lewy bodies (DLB) is the sec-
ond most common cause of neurodegenerative dementia,
followed by Alzheimer ’s disease (AD). The pathological hall-
mark of DLB is Lewy bodies and Lewy neurites that contain
aggregated α-synuclein in neurons. DLB is frequently associ-
ated with AD neuropathological change. In addition, other
neuropathologic processes characterized by the accumulation
of misfolded proteins, such as tau, amyloid, α-synuclein, and
TDP-43 are observed. This study aimed to determine the fre-
quency of copathologies and assess their impact on the rate
of cognitive decline in patients with DLB.
