The mean follow-up was 4.1 /C62.9 years. Braak neuro ﬁbril-
lary tangle stage was 0-III in 26 and IV-VI in 36 cases. Thal
amyloid phase was 0-2 in 18 and 3-5 in 44 cases. CAA was
observed in 46 cases (74%). The frequencies of LATE-NC
stage 1, 2, and 3 were 31%, 16%, and 8%, respectively. The
frequency of concurrent pathologies increased with increasing
age, except for CAA. When DLB patients were divided into
two groups (i.e., with and without AD), the frequency of
CAA increased with increasing age in LBD without AD, but
did not change in LBD with AD. The coexistence of AD or
CAA, but not LATE-NC ( in any stages), was associated with
greater mean annual decline on the MMSE, DRS, or GLDS.
