that they have advance directives. Compared to stroke survi-
vors without advance directives, those with advance direc-
tives were older (median age 72 vs. 61 years; p<0.001), and
were more likely to be White (91.2% vs. 75.9%, p<0.001),
male (58.6% vs. 46.5%, p=0.015), higher educated
(p<0.001), and report higher annual income (p=0.011).
