Background/Objective: Severe intracerebral hemorrhage
(ICH) and acute ischemic stroke (AIS) carry high mortality,
and a majority of patients alive at 3 months are functionally
dependent. This study aimed to assess the accuracy of early
estimates of long-term outcomes among surrogate decision
makers of patients with severe stroke.
