rogates of patients who survived the index hospitalization were
contacted at 3 months for a blinded telephone mRS.
Results: Between November 20, 2020, and May
24, 2021, 29 surrogates completed the survey. Of the
29 patients, 9 presented with ICH (median ICH score
3, IQR 2-4) and 20 with AIS (median NIHSS 21, IQR
19.5-27.5). The median surrogate estimated mRS was
4 (IQR 3-4), while the median observed patient mRS was
5 (IQR 4-6). Although 86.2% of surrogates estimated that
their respective family member was alive at 3 months, only
51.7% of patients were observed alive. Surrogate estimated
vs. observed 3-month mRS ≤3 was 41.4% vs. 17.2%, and
estimated vs. observed 3-month mRS ≤4 was 82.8%
vs. 34.5%, respectively. The median difference between
