Results: A 39-year-old Native American woman
(Kickapoo tribe) reportedly on venlafaxine presented with a
severe headache followed by status epilepticus. She had left-
hemispheric vasogenic edema and frontal convexity SAH.
She started IV glucocorticoids for empiric treatment of vas-
culitis. Digital subtraction a ngiography detected multiple
unruptured intracranial aneurysms and diffuse focal segmen-
tal vasoconstriction of intracranial cortical arteries involving
anterior, middle, and posterior cerebral arteries. She started
Verapamil 60mg q/6h. CSF and serum autoimmune studies
were negative for infection or vasculitis. EEG did not iden-
tify seizures. The repeated image on day 10 revealed wors-
