ciated with neuro ﬁbrillary tangles, and up-regulated in stroke-
injured cortical neurons resulting in selective axonal remo-
deling and site-speci ﬁc phosphorylation of Tau in-vivo. The
present study aims to investigate MARK4 inhibition as a novel
therapeutic target for Tau accumulation in vascular cognitive
impairment. Twenty-three novel MARK4 inhibitors were
designed by systematic chemical subgroup iteration around the
active site of a known non-speci ﬁc MARK enzyme inhibitor.
New chemical structures were screened by in silico binding
afﬁnity and for inhibition of enzymatic activity using a short
peptide phosphorylation activity assay. Candidate inhibitors
were screened for their ability to block MARK4-mediated
