strates signi ﬁcant detection of pSer-262 Tau peptides (0%
vs. 17.7%, p= 0.005). For inhibitor screening, a custom
AlphaLISA was designed to demonstrate signi ﬁcant quantita-
tive detection of Tau phosphorylation by MARK4
(660 /C6181.1 vs. 4633 /C6234.7, p = 0.0002). Using this
multi-stage in-vitro assay, site-speci ﬁcM A R K 4a c t i v i t yo n
human full-length Tau is dependent on inhibitor dosage and
chemical subgroup structure. Once successful inhibitors of
MARK4-mediated Tau phosphorylation are identi ﬁed, these
molecules may be considered for rigorous pre-clinical testing in
a VCID model to prevent the Tau aggregation characteristic of
vascular brain injury.
