therapy and secondary stroke prevention. However, how lon-
gitudinal outcomes of patients differ when stroke etiology is
undetermined (i.e. cryptogenic), despite a complete workup,
is not well characterized. This study aims to determine the
associations between longitudinal outcomes, de ﬁned as stroke
recurrence, non-stroke related hospital readmission, and
death, and IS subtype (cryptogenic versus other).
