the Johns Hopkins Hospital (2017-2019) were followed lon-
gitudinally for adverse events. The National Death Index,
Chesapeake Regional Information System for our Patients
(CRISP), and Johns Hopkins medical records were used to
determine IS recurrence, non-stroke hospital readmission,
and death. IS subtype was classi ﬁed per TOAST algorithm
by masked reviewers. Logistic regression was used to deter-
mine the association between cryptogenic IS and recurrent
IS, or hospital admission, each in separate models. A Cox
proportional hazards model was used to evaluate the time
from initial stroke to recurrent stroke by IS subtype with
competing risk for re-hospitalization or death. Models were
adjusted for sex, age, race, and IS volume.
