MA, Ahmed Z. Obeidat, MD, PhD. Medical College of
Wisconsin, Milwaukee, WI, USA.
Introduction: Epilepsy affects approximately 50 million peo-
ple of all ages worldwide and is characterized by recurrent
unprovoked epileptic seizures. Advancements in management
have led to development of brivaracetam (BRV) and
levetiracetam (LEV). BRV is a newer AED that is more
