naire to assess stroke awareness, a 46-item COVID survey to
assess lifestyle changes, and a 15-item diet screener. Partici-
pants were recruited at random from a booth on site.
Results: The majority of those surveyed were black
(n=36/40) with most being between the ages of 30-44
(n=33/40). Participants were identi ﬁed as male (n=18) or
female (n=22). Participants endorsed decreased physical activ-
