Shadi Ghourchian, MD , Ann L. Gruber-Baldini, PhD,
Professor, Sunita Shakya, PhD, Stephen G. Reich, MD,
Friedrich R. von Coelln, MD, Joseph M. Savitt, MD, Lisa
M. Shulman, MD. University of Maryland, Baltimore,
MD, USA.
Introduction: Spirituality and religious beliefs are important
for coping with medical conditions. The dopaminergic sys-
tem is involved in reward behavior, and its dysfunction in
