Background: Primary CNS lymphoma can have myriad pre-
sentations. Based on the recent criteria for autoimmune
encephalitis, AE should be suspected in patients with sub-
acute onset of memory de ﬁcits, seizures or psychiatric mani-
festations suggesting involvement of limbic system that
exhibits bilateral abnormalities on MRI or EEG showing epi-
leptic and/or slow-wave activity involving the temporal lobes.
