scattered non-enhancing white matter lesions mainly in the
subcortical region, with some periventricular lesions but no
T1 black holes or corpus callosal involvement. MRI C&T
spine were unremarkable. CT Angiography of the head and
neck were normal. ENT documented bilateral sensorineural
hearing loss. A normal optical-computed-tomography con-
ﬁrmed no optic neuritis. Retinal angiography ruled out
branched retinal artery occlusion. Serum TSH, B12, folate,
copper, ceruloplasmin, protein S and C, autoimmune anti-
body screen, anti-aquaporin-4-antibody, antithrombin III,
DRV VT screen, homocysteine, factor V Leiden, plasma
amino acids and urine organic acids, plasma-VLCFA, bile
acids, pyruvate and lactate levels were all normal. CSF did
not show exclusive oligoclonal bands. Repeat MRI brain in
