Objective: To evaluate deoxycytidine kinase (dCK) as a
potential therapeutic target for multiple sclerosis (MS).
Background: MS is a neuroin ﬂammatory disease caused
by immune attack on myelin in the central nervous system
(CNS). Aberrant T cell proliferation, akin to MS, is associ-
ated with increased nucleoside salvage pathway (NSP)
