Background: Vogt Koyangi Harada (VKH) Syndrome is a
rare, idiopathic, autoimmune disease characterized by bilat-
eral ocular involvement. Commonly seen ocular ﬁndings
include granulomatous uveitis and serious retinal detach-
ments. Patient can also present with neurological, auditory,
and skin manifestations such as headaches, tinnitus, hearing
loss, vertigo, alopecia, and vitiligo.
