headache and left ear pain. Patient-reported that the headache
started a month ago after her cataract surgery. The patient was
currently on steroid taper for her recent cataract surgery. Physi-
cal examination did not show any abnormal motor or sensory
deﬁcits, coordination, or gait instability. Laboratory work-up
was unremarkable without any signs of infection. MRI brain
shows nonspeci ﬁc non-enhancing periventricular lesions,
which are also likely associated with VKH syndrome. Given
the absence of any new focal neurological de ﬁcits and MRI
ﬁndings her headache, dizziness, and left ear pain were likely
