noma status post left nephroureterectomy, four cycles of radiation,
and two doses of Pembrolizumab presented to the hospital
complaining of dyspnea, leg weakness, and severe myalgias. Simi-
l a rs y m p t o m sa f t e rh e rﬁrst dose of Pembrolizumab remitted with
Prednisone. She presented with markedly elevated creatinine
kinase, liver enzymes, and troponins without evidence of acute
ischemia. Diagnosis of Pembro lizumab-induced myasthenia
gravis-like syndrome with presumed Triple M Syndrome (myas-
thenia gravis, myositis, probable myocarditis) was made after the
onset of right-sided eye ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, and dysphagia.
