received two doses of IVIG with no improvement but signiﬁcant
worsening. She decompensated, required intubation, and was
transferred to the ICU. Plasmapheresis (PLEX) was initiated every
other day for 5 sessions; she showed improvement and was suc-
cessfully extubated. However, she subsequently suffered an aspira-
tion event, requiring reintubat ion. Rituximab was infused for
long term immunosuppression, but due to its delayed onset of
action of a few weeks, PLEX was restarted. She developed severe
thrombocytopenia and anemia, re quiring multiple transfusions.
