Illinois University School of Medicine, Spring ﬁeld, IL, USA.
Objective: Hereditary diffuse leukoencephalopathy with spher-
oids (HDLS) is a rare disease that is associated with demyelin-
ation and axonal spheroids, or axonal swellings within the
abnormal myelin sheath. We present a case of HDLS in a
31-year old male with a proven diagnosis via genetic testing.
Case Report: A 31-year old male with a history of depres-
sion, anxiety, and tremors presented with progressively
