ApolipoproteinA1 (ApoA1) is a main protein moiety in high-
density lipoprotein particles and has been extensively known
to be involved in cholesterol transport and to confer protec-
tion against atherosclerosis. Alteration in brain cholesterol
homeostasis may be a contributing factor for Parkinson ’s dis-
ease (PD), and we have previously shown that ApoA1 levels
associate with age at disease onset, as well as disease severity.
