homogenates (BH. frontal lobe and amygdala) from
22 patients with different LRP distributions (none=4,
amygdala-predominant=10, or limbic/neocortical=8) were
analyzed by αS-SAA. BHs were analyzed at a 10
-8 dilution to
avoid assay interference in a kinetic αS-SAA(4), while CSF
samples were analyzed using the clinical assay (SynTap).
Ampliﬁed products were digested with proteinase K (PK) and
analyzed by SDS-PAGE. Formalin- ﬁxed paraf ﬁn-embedded
sections from frontal lobe and amygdala were
immunohistochemically stained for phosphorylated αSyn
(81A) and rated on a severity scale from 0-3 (0:none, 1:mild,
2:moderate, 3:severe).
