SAA negative in CSF (9/10 antemortem and 4/7 postmortem
samples negative). The electrophoretic pattern of PK-treated
αSyn seeds ampli ﬁed from CSF of limbic/neocortical and
amygdala-predominant cases was the same as the pattern
described for PD and different from the MSA pattern( 5).
Limbic/neocortical cases had αSyn seeding activity in frontal
lobe and amygdala; however, αSyn seeds were detected in the
amygdala of 50% of the amygdala-predominant cases, and
20% presented αSyn seeds in frontal lobe. Higher degrees of
αSyn pathology by immunohistochemistry was associated
with greater likelihood of positive seeding ( χ
2=17.7,
p=0.007).
