Background: Higher CSF and plasma neuro ﬁlament light
chain (NFL) levels, which re ﬂect axonal damage in both the
CNS and PNS, are seen in several acquired and inherited
polyneuropathies but have not been studied in HIV distal
sensory polyneuropathy (DSP). We evaluated NFL levels in
CSF and plasma in DSP in people with HIV (PWH) from
two independent cohorts and in PWoH.
Methods: Cohort 1 consisted of PWH from the CHARTER
Aging Study. Cohort 2 consisted of PWH and PWoH from the
HIV Neurobehavioral Research Center (HNRC). We performed
the same standardized clinical evaluation of DSP signs and symp-
toms using graded scales in both cohorts. We used two different
immunoassays to measure NFL in cerebrospinal ﬂuid (CSF) for
the two cohorts and for plasma as well in Cohort 2.
Results: Cohort 1 was 111 PWH, mean+/-SD age 56.8+/-
8.32 years, 15.3% female, 38.7% black, 49.6% white, cur-
rent CD4 (median, IQR) 532 (295, 785), nadir CD4
95 (15, 199), 98.2% on ART, 83.5% with plasma viral load
suppressed. Log10 CSF NFL was higher in those with more
than 2 signs of DSP (3.15 /C60.174) compared to those with
1 sign (3.13+/-0.249) and those with 0 signs (3.01+/-0.190,
p=0.0108). Cohort 2 consisted of 233 PWH, age 57.3+/-
6.71 years, 15.9% female, 16.9% black, 658.4% non-
Hispanic white, current CD4 432 (267, 646), nadir CD4
52 (12, 190), 100 % on ART, 100% with plasma viral load
suppressed; and 51 PWoH, age 58.4+/-6.68 years, 41.2%
female, 18.0% black, 52.0% non-Hispanic white. Log10
CSF NFL was higher in those with more than 1 sign of DSP
(6.77+/-0.669) compared to those with 1 sign (6.54+/-
0.577) and those with 0 signs (6.49+/-0.662, p=0.0035).
Corresponding levels for log10 plasma NFL were 2.72+/-
0.690 versus 2.55 /C60.492 versus 2.35+/-0.530, p=6.60e-6).
The observed relationships were not explained by confounds
including demographics, viral suppression, nadir and current
CD4, diabetes mellitus and lifetime alcohol use disorder.
Conclusions: In two independent datasets, both plasma
and CSF NFL were elevated in PWH and PWoH with DSP.
