with the diagnosis. Biopsies are not requisite for diagnosis of
CLIPPERS syndrome but are helpful in the exclusion of
alternative pathologies. This patient did receive a biopsy of
the pons which revealed T cells in perivascular foci, a ﬁnding
characteristic of the disease. This case demonstrates the vari-
