analysis of channel kinetics, and simulation of endplate
potential (EPP).
Results: We identiﬁed a novel deletion of the third residue
in Cys-loop of the AChR ε subunit ( εE131del) in 4 CMS
patients. Three patients are homozygous for εE131del,
whereas one patient has εE24Gfs*3 in the second allele.
εE131del reduced receptor expression to 33% of wild-type
but prolonged the duration of channel opening burst
2.65-fold mainly due to increased gating ef ﬁciency. Com-
pared to the control EPP, the simulated EPP amplitude with
εE131del was reduced by 3-fold. Experimental deletion of
12 other residues in the ε subunit Cys-loop reduced receptor
expression to 20 to 40% of wild-type, but had different
effects on channel kinetics. The ﬁrst 7 and the 11th residues
increased burst duration 2- to 4-fold, whereas the remaining
6 residues (highly conserved εD138 and its upstream and
downstream residues) decreased burst duration 3- to 4-fold.
Deleting the 3rd Cys-loop residues of non- ε subunits
corresponding to εE131 resulted in nonfunctional in the α
subunit, had no effect in the β subunit, and reduced opening
burst duration in the δ subunit 2-fold. Deletion of each indi-
vidual Cys-loop residue in non- ε subunits reduced receptor
expression to a similar extent to deletions in the ε subunit.
Conclusions: We traced 4 CMS patients to a novel reces-
sive mutation in the AChR ε subunit. The prolongation of
channel opening episodes is insuf ﬁcient to compensate for
the reduced expression of the mutant. The length of Cys-
loop is a determinant of AChR expression, but it affects
AChR activation in a subunit speci ﬁc manner. The contribu-
tions of individual residues in the Cys-loop to channel open-
ing are position dependent.
M277. LUMINESCE: A Phase 3 Study Evaluating
Satralizumab, a Therapeutic Recycling Antibody
Targeting the IL-6 Receptor, in Patients with Generalized
Myasthenia Gravis
Henry Kaminski, MD
1, Chongbo Zhao, PhD 2, Gerd Meyer
zu Hörste, PhD 3, Kevin C. O ’Connor, PhD 4, Gaëlle
Klingelschmitt, Msc 5, Petranka Krumova, PhD 5, Stuart Bolt,
Msc6, Ivana Vodopivec, PhD 5, Siân Lennon-Chrimes, PhD 6,
