Temozolomide (TMZ) is a chemotherapeutic agent that has
been the ﬁrst-line standard of care for the aggressive brain
cancer glioblastoma (GBM) since 2005. Though initially
beneﬁcial, TMZ-resistance is universal and second-line inter-
ventions are an unmet clinical need. Here we took advan-
