Pediatric brain tumors are associated with speci ﬁca g e so f
onset, tumor locations and molecular alterations. These alter-
ations are often in epigenetic regulators thought to contribute
to a “stalled development” phenotype. Modeling these tumors
is frustrated by their remarkable context speci ﬁcity. Human
organoid systems are uniquely poised to address some of the
limitations of other approaches. Here, we describe an inducible
transgenic cerebral organoid system harboring canonical diffuse
midline glioma (DMG) mutations. This model reproducibly
undergoes malignant transformation in vitro and in vivo that
is dependent on persistent transgenic oncogene expression.
