Neurological symptoms are common during COVID-19
infection and continue for many patients following recovery.
Given the heterogeneity of self-reported symptoms and their
subjective severity, clinicians also require objective measures
with which to identify and treat neurological de ﬁcits in
acutely recovered but chronically impaired COVID-19 (long-
